"id":"floor_division",
"source":"floor_division.py",
"code":"import sys\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    raw = sys.stdin.read()\n    data = raw.split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n\n    n = int(data[0])\n    total = 0\n    blocks = 0\n    d = 1\n    while d <= n:\n        q = n // d\n        last = n // q\n        count = last - d + 1\n        total += q * count\n        blocks += 1\n        d = last + 1\n\n    print(total)\n    print(blocks)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n",
"alt":"The loop reads a block start d, finds the shared quotient q and the last d with that quotient, adds q times the block's size to the total, and jumps to the start of the next block.",
